# Independent factual scope review of the v4 preparation

No concrete factual or scope blocker was found in the reviewed report, terminal selection, and publication index. The fixed selection contains exactly five lifecycle runs, six primary performance runs, and the first default-native failure: 11 controller PASS results and one exit-1 failure before any window. The index contains 13 capsules including the 122-file support capsule; archive contents were not revalidated by this review.

All original primary table rows remain present after whitespace normalization. The report preserves both adjacent throughput gains, raw/native drift, the slower mixed throughput and worse TTFT/P99 relative to the synchronous native reference, the post-N1 calibrated supplementary scope, and mixed native/plugin token divergence. The prior independent token-review boundary is also retained.

Lifecycle wording agrees with the prior trace-based reviews: 22-block cancellation headroom is separate from 20-block pressure; partial/full ACK and physical reuse identities are correct; real D preemption preserves pending P ownership in the grouped 20-block case. The earlier raw20 suite remains FAIL. Native SIGTERM fallback and the grouped pressure run's additional SIGKILL count 1 are explicitly retained, without a globally graceful-shutdown claim.

The failed default-native v1 has zero windows, returned shutdown, and the exact wrapper-class readback failure. Existing logs support the stated 16 CPU checks, six independently repeated wrapper checks, and copied-layout dry-run. Default-native v2 is described only as preparation; its measured results, actual profiler and paired quality outcomes are excluded. No universal performance, semantic-quality, physical-overlap, or public-download qualification is claimed.

The accompanying JSON binds the reviewed bytes and records unchanged-input checks. This review did not validate archives, contact GitHub, run models/devices/tests, or alter frozen producers, attempts, or reports.
